{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>For a hand upon the throne of Yah.</b> When there is strength in the hand of Israel to establish for themselves a king who will sit upon the throne of the Holy One, blessed be He, in the manner of 'and Solomon sat upon the throne of YHWH as king' — then there will be war of YHWH against Amalek." "<b>A hand.</b> In the sense of strength and dominion, as it is written, 'Saul came from Carmel and behold he was setting up a hand for himself,' and it says, 'as he went to turn back his hand at the river Euphrates.' And 'throne' is in the sense of kingship, as it is written, 'and his throne shall be greater than your throne.' Another interpretation: 'For a hand upon the throne of Yah' — the hand of Amalek is upon His throne, of the Holy One, blessed be He; this is Jerusalem. <b>War of YHWH against Amalek</b> — upon him the war is incumbent. And on this the paytan founded: 'Remember, pray, the day of your dwelling' — when Titus burned Jerusalem; therefore it is phrased 'to him.' That is, upon you the matter is incumbent to do it. And this is the allusion of the writing מחה (I will blot) and the writing תמחה (you shall blot): before he stretched out his hand against the throne — תמחה, you shall blot; after he stretched out his hand against the throne — אמחה, I will blot. And this is the Jerusalem above, which is called 'throne,' as it is written, 'In that day they shall call Jerusalem the throne of YHWH.' <b>Shelima, the order of the portion Beshalah.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "The paytanic citation 'נא זכור יום זבולך' does not correspond to any known standard piyyut; it is translated as it stands. The word שלימא at the very end appears to be a colophon marking the completion of the commentary on the sedra."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:26.605700278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}